      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:ej0iki'
    '|a||Real against real, the council lost. Put the whole comparison on one grid: market or state, ideal or real.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9560
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||The nirvana fallacy runs along this diagonal: a real market against an ideal state.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1nv4fao'
    '|b||But hold on. Doesn''t that hand every lobby an excuse? Propose any rule, and someone says the government might fail.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6760
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:byxvnl'
    '|a||It would, if you only ran it one way. Comparing a real state with a perfect market is the same mistake, backwards.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:k2tiql'
    '|b||And real states do win sometimes. In 2003 London began charging drivers to enter its centre, and in the first year delays there fell by about thirty percent.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8960
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:b52ck6'
    '|a||While Mexico City''s ban left the air no cleaner. The same kind of problem, two real states, opposite results.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:wu0999'
    '|b||So the honest comparison is this bottom row, one case at a time.':
